# Hardware firmware (plan §12).
#
# Only firmware that Debian distributes is included. Redistribution licensing is handled by
# Debian's non-free-firmware component, which the archive definition in
# config/archives/astraos.list.chroot enables (plan §23).
#
# WHY THIS LIST IS EXPLICIT
# -------------------------
# live-build can install firmware for you: its firmware stage scans the archive and installs
# every package whose name begins with "firmware-". That is switched off in auto/config
# (--firmware-chroot false), because the sweep:
#
#   * defeats this file, so the image depends on whatever the archive happens to contain at
#     build time rather than on a reviewed selection;
#   * pulls in firmware-b43-installer and firmware-b43legacy-installer from contrib, whose
#     post-install scripts download Broadcom firmware from the internet. That download failed
#     and stopped a build after several gigabytes had already been installed.
#
# Everything the sweep used to provide is therefore listed here by name. Adding a package
# here is a deliberate act; nothing arrives by accident.
#
# Untested hardware: nothing in this list has been verified on physical hardware.
# See docs/HARDWARE_COMPATIBILITY.md and docs/KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md.

# Generic bundles
firmware-linux-free
firmware-linux-nonfree
firmware-misc-nonfree

# Wi-Fi
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-atheros
firmware-realtek
firmware-brcm80211
firmware-mediatek
firmware-ti-connectivity
firmware-libertas
firmware-ipw2x00
firmware-zd1211
firmware-siano
firmware-qcom-soc
firmware-qcom-media
firmware-samsung
wireless-regdb
# NOTE: there is no firmware-rtlwifi package in Debian; RTL Wi-Fi firmware ships in
# firmware-realtek (listed above).
#
# NOTE: Broadcom's older chips (the b43 driver) are NOT covered. Their firmware is not
# redistributable as a Debian package — Debian ships installers that download it instead,
# which cannot run in a build chroot and cannot be trusted to work offline. A user with such
# a card installs firmware-b43-installer on the installed system with a network connection.
# See docs/HARDWARE_COMPATIBILITY.md.

# Wired networking
firmware-bnx2
firmware-bnx2x
firmware-cavium
firmware-marvell-prestera
firmware-myricom
firmware-netronome
firmware-netxen
firmware-qlogic

# Graphics
firmware-amd-graphics
firmware-intel-graphics
firmware-nvidia-graphics
firmware-nvidia-gsp
firmware-nvidia-tesla-535-gsp
firmware-cirrus

# Audio and misc
firmware-sof-signed
firmware-intel-sound
firmware-intel-misc
firmware-ivtv
alsa-firmware-loaders
